\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. HERE, O my Lord, I see Thee face to face;
\par Here would I touch and handle things unseen,
\par Here grasp with firmer hand the eternal grace,
\par And all my weariness upon Thee lean.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Here would I feed upon the bread of God,
\par Here drink with Thee the royal wine of heaven;
\par Here would I lay aside each earthly load,
\par Here taste afresh the calm of sin forgiven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. This is the hour of banquest and of song;
\par This is the heavenly table spread for me;
\par Here let me feast, and, feasting, still prolong
\par The brief, bright hour of fellowship with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I have no help but Thine; nor do I need
\par Another arm save Thine to lean upon;
\par It is enough, my Lord, enough indeed;
\par My strength is in Thy might, Thy might alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Mine in the sin, but Thine the righteousness;
\par Mine is the guilt, but Thine the cleansing blood;
\par Here is my robe, my refuge, and my peace-
\par Thy blood, Thy righteousness, O Lord, my God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Feast after feast thus comes and passes by,
\par Yet, passing, points to the glad feast above,
\par Giving sweet foretaste of the festal joy,
\par The Lamb's great bridal feast of bliss and love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

